RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, these functions return the natural logarithm of _x.

       If _x is a NaN, a NaN is returned.

       If _x is 1, the result is +0.

       If _x is positive infinity, positive infinity is returned.

       If  _x  is  zero,  then  a  pole  error occurs, and the functions return
       -HHUUGGEE__VVAALL, -HHUUGGEE__VVAALLFF, or -HHUUGGEE__VVAALLLL, respectively.

       If _x is negative (including negative infinity), then a domain error oc‐
       curs, and a NaN (not a number) is returned.

